<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Overview">Overview</span></h3>
<p>This page details character save game values.
</p><p><br />
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="File_Locations">File Locations</span></h3>
<p>For savegame locations under Vista they are, by default under "&lt;user's document directory&gt;\\Bioware\\Dragon Age\\Characters\\&lt;Name of the Character the save is for&gt;\\&lt;save slot&gt;\\&lt;savename&gt;.das". As the save name is part of the save file name (though not the folders) it should be pretty easy to find the proper folder name provided one named one's save something distinguishable.
</p><p>If you get an "Toolset out of memory"-error when trying to open your savegame there is a temporary unofficial workaround available <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="http://social.bioware.com/11689/blog/707/">here</a>, if your system is equipped with 4+gb ram.
</p>
<h3><span class="mw-headline" id="Player_Character_Stats">Player Character Stats</span></h3>
<p>Found under SAVEGAME_PLAYERCHAR-&gt;SAVEGAME_PLAYERCHAR_CHAR-&gt;SAVEGAME_CREATURE_STATS-&gt;SAVEGAME_STATLIST
</p><p>For party members the same values should hold. Navigate to:
SAVEGAME_PARTYLIST-&gt;SAVEGAME_PARTYPOOLMEMBERS-&gt;&lt;number&gt;-&gt;SAVEGAME_CREATURE_STATS-&gt;SAVEGAME_STATLIST
</p><p>Note: The following values are recorded by the game in a FIFO order, meaning the moment the game needs to generate a specific key, it will do that.
</p>
